  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted; acc 0.678). With PCA, the image encoder choice (resnet50 vs ViT-L) was nearly irrelevant (0.639 vs 0.635), but that comparison used a linear PCA representation. scvi_n200 produces a learned latent embedding that may interact differently with a more expressive image encoder. config_037 is a clean single-variable extension of the current best (only swapping resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l), directly testing whether the image modality is underutilized with resnet50 when paired with the superior RNA encoder. This is the highest-value next experiment because it isolates one important design axis, builds on the strongest evidence (scvi_n200 + avgpool + weighted), and the result will either confirm resnet50 sufficiency (focusing future effort on aggregation/fusion) or reveal a meaningful image-encoder gain that opens a new promising direction—all with minimal risk of a wasted run."
